course: dictionary
lesson: 2453
title: Dangerous and danger signs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word dangerous means able or likely to hurt someone, or full of risk. Look at the words around it for clues. «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» The list tells you what could go wrong: knives can cut, hot pans can burn, and slippery floors can make you fall.
explain: Knowing why something is dangerous helps you avoid it even in a new situation. «Water with impurities, like tap water, can conduct electricity, so water and electricity are dangerous together.» The clue is the word together: each one is less risky alone, but together they can hurt you. Ask yourself what could hurt you, and the context will show you.
fact: Dangerous is an adjective, so it describes a noun: «a dangerous road» or «a dangerous game».
fact: «Dangerous» means able or likely to hurt or harm someone, or full of risk.
fact: Warning signs and labels often say «Danger», so you can spot dangerous things before you touch them.
fact: Dangerous things include traffic, deep water, fire, electricity and bleach.
fact: Saying no to something dangerous can feel hard, but going along to fit in is how many children get hurt.
exercise: «Walk, never run, in the kitchen: knives, hot pans and slippery floors make running dangerous.» What does dangerous mean here? | *Able or likely to hurt you | Loud and noisy | Very fast and fun | Clean and tidy
exercise: Which of these is a dangerous thing to play near? | A bench in the park | *Deep water | A picture book | A soft pillow
exercise: Tap water can conduct electricity. Why is water and electricity together dangerous? | Water makes electricity sweeter | Electricity turns water into sugar | *Together they can hurt you | Water and electricity make a warm bath
test: Which word would you see on a sign for something dangerous? | *Danger | Hello | Welcome
test: «Knowing why something is dangerous helps you avoid it even in a new situation.» What does this tell us? | Dangerous means fun | You never need to think about risk | *Understanding the risk helps you stay safe | Dangerous things are always the same
exam: Why is a wet, icy roof dangerous to climb? | *It could make you slip and fall | It is very short | It is painted blue | It has a lovely view
